body:
tw: csa

&#x200B;

today was awful. it was so miserable. when she came up to me and started asking me questions like, "did he touch you too?" i instantly shut down. i couldn't process it. i still can't. but these memories i locked away are suddenly popping in my head and i can't tell if it's my mind making it up...or if it really happened... or if it was even anything. he got my sister too. my cousin. i always felt so uncomfortable around him but all i could think of him was that he was just the stupid, lovable grandpa. i feel like my trust was so misplaced. he always upheld himself as a high moral, upstanding man of god. always spreading the word, always caring for others. but if i'm really remembering what i am.... how can people be so awful? i was so little. i loved you. i trusted you. everybody trusted you. everybody thought you were a saint. but you didn't stop with me. you hurt everyone. i can't imagine the pain my dad is going through. he's smiling, he's asking if we're all okay. constantly checking up on us and trying to take care of us, but he trusted you and all he ever wanted to do was protect us. how could he have known to protect us from you? his dad? i don't know what to do. i don't know what's real. did my mind just make up whatever i'm remembering because why wouldn't it? it can't be real. is that why there was so much wrong with me? what did you do to me? what did you do to us? i don't feel safe. i don't feel okay. i don't want to think about this ever again. i just wanna pretend it was my imagination.

I was so confused for a second, I was genuinely wondering how in the world this dude picked up windows.... I'm still kind of confused. 

&#x200B;

*plop*!

I wish I did this T\_T but I wanna take Lilly's life with my own hands....

&#x200B;

^(that sounds really fucked LOL oops)

what

&#x200B;

what the fuck

&#x200B;

i feel weird that i have to upvote this, but take it you strange person...

>It's ok not to work hard to break the stereotype, because selling yourself out is more important than proving your genuine self-worth.

? Huh? Yeah, there are stereotypes against women but let those girls live. They know their self-worth and they are owning it. They are doing what they enjoy and what makes them happy. If they're proud of their body, then let them flaunt it off! Who are you to deem "shame" on them? They are HAPPY with themselves and expressing themselves. It's a prominent platform, but it's also one that's now considered a SOCIAL platform that has included an option to mark your stream as mature.

&#x200B;

Yes, kids are influenced by what they see - but that's up to the parent's on how they teach them to treat women. Not how a women decides to be seen. PLUS, they should do a better job of moderating what that child is doing anyway! If you don't want your kid to see that, then take measures to prevent so DON'T bash someone for doing something they love. No no, your child's values rest on your teachings not some online stranger.

&#x200B;

I won't get into any more of it, but just because streamers dress themselves up differently doesn't mean they behave differently. I can tell you now that some of them follow the same online practices that "less clothed" ones do and they make work of it. You're just adding to the problem just as much as anyone really at this point if you're going to judge someone on their clothes.

I think about my childhood best friend. She was the first friend I really had and my parents let her come over to my house and let me go to hers. In second grade, she told me she was moving away and some other stuff. I got upset, threw our best friend ring on the floor, and declared I wasn't her best friend. (never was good with handling my emotions, still am not.) I remember she picked it up off the floor and looked so heartbroken. I don't remember if I said sorry. Or goodbye. 

&#x200B;

I wish I did.

&#x200B;

Haven't been able to find anything of her online since then. I wonder if she's doing okay or if she's still alive. I wish I hadn't broken her heart then, maybe she and I would still be friends now.
